 In 盛る, 盛 writes も and る is okurigana, the kana ending that follows the kanji. In 盛り and 盛ん, 盛 writes さか; the り of 盛り and the ん of 盛ん complete the words. The same さか.る reading also belongs to the verb 盛る read さかる, JMdict "to become vigorous; to gain force; to become more active," which has no word article yet. In 花盛り はなざかり, "flowers in full bloom; time of year in which flowers are in full bloom," 盛り is read ざかり, its さかり with a voiced sound.
 
